<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Keeps this Mac awake through US market hours, on weekdays.

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  Alpaca does not support bracket/OCO orders on options - confirmed against the
  real API. There is no server-side stop-loss. `monitor_exits.py`, polling every
  15 minutes from this machine, is therefore the ONLY mechanism protecting an
  open position.

  That mechanism has already failed once for exactly this reason: the job failed
  11 times in a row one afternoon, not from a permissions or config fault, but
  because the Mac was asleep and launchd only fired it during brief maintenance
  wake-ups - too short for Wi-Fi to reconnect before the network call timed out.
  Each failure timestamp matched the system sleep log to the second.

  Until now, staying awake depended on someone being at the keyboard. This makes
  it a configuration instead.

  WHAT IT DOES, AND WHAT IT CANNOT DO
  `caffeinate -dimu` prevents idle, display and disk sleep for the duration. It
  runs 15:20 to 22:05 local time (Europe/Zurich, CEST = UTC+2), which covers
  13:30-20:00 UTC with ten minutes on either side.

  It can only keep the machine awake - it CANNOT wake a machine that is already
  asleep. Waking requires a scheduled power event, which needs administrator
  rights:

      sudo pmset repeat wakeorpoweron MTWRF 15:15:00

  Run that once, and the two together close the gap: pmset wakes the machine at
  15:15, this agent keeps it awake until 22:05.

  StartCalendarInterval fires at 15:20 on each weekday (1=Monday .. 5=Friday).
  If the machine is asleep at that moment, launchd runs the job at the next
  wake instead - which is precisely why the pmset line above matters.

  INSTALL   cp launchagents/com.hindsightalpha.market-hours-awake.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
            launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.hindsightalpha.market-hours-awake.plist
  STOP      launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.hindsightalpha.market-hours-awake
  STATUS    launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.hindsightalpha.market-hours-awake
-->
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
    <key>Label</key><string>com.hindsightalpha.market-hours-awake</string>

    <!-- Duree portee de 24300 s a 25200 s le 28/08/2026. A 24300 la fenetre
     se fermait a 22:05:00, l'instant EXACT ou le dernier instantane du
     jour est programme. Le verrou de veille expirait donc a la seconde
     ou la derniere preuve de la seance devait s'ecrire. Le systeme ne
     s'endort pas instantanement, donc le job passait probablement ; se
     reposer sur ce probablement est precisement ce que ce depot traque
     ailleurs. 25200 s ferme a 22:20 et laisse 15 minutes de marge. -->
<key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/caffeinate</string>
        <string>-dimu</string>
        <string>-t</string>
        <string>25200</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>1</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>15</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>2</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>15</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>3</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>15</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>4</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>15</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Weekday</key><integer>5</integer><key>Hour</key><integer>15</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
    </array>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/s-pap/hindsight-alpha/market_hours_awake.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/s-pap/hindsight-alpha/market_hours_awake.log</string>
</dict></plist>
